<title>MOLDOVA: Moldovan 28 and 91-day T-bill yields rise.</title>
<headline>Moldovan 28 and 91-day T-bill yields rise.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised yield on Moldovan 28-day Treasury bills rose to 29.32 percent on Tuesday from 26.60 percent at the previous auction on December 3, a National Bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The yield on 91-day T-bills rose to 27.88 percent annual from 26.51 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the 28-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>						 Dec 10	  Dec 3</p>
<p>    Issue volume			   3.00 million lei  4.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Denominations			  1,000 lei     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand			 3.67 million	3.69 million</p>
<p>    Volume sold			    3.00 million	3.64 million</p>
<p>    Yield				    29.32 pct     26.60 pct</p>
<p>    Price				    97.8 pct	98.0 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids			  97.8-98.6 pct 98.0-98.7pct</p>
<p>    Maturity				 Jan 9, 1997   Jan 2, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the three-month T-bill auction:</p>
<p>						 Dec 10	  Dec 3</p>
<p>    Issue volume			   10.00 million lei 12.00 millionlei</p>
<p>    Denominations			  1,000 lei     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand			 6.60 million	16.26 million</p>
<p>    Volume sold			    6.40 million	12.00 million</p>
<p>    Yield				    27.88 pct     26.51 pct</p>
<p>    Price				    93.5 pct	93.8 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids			  93.5-95.0 pct 93.8-97.5pct</p>
<p>    Maturity				 March 13,1997 March 6,1997</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
